{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdsYWeLc2hj1tEHasVsbW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have everything I need. This is the `isolated-child` family: my in-session nodes are **observe-evidence** and **propose-child**; validate-child, create-child, child-return, verify-integration, and return-result are root-executed. (The `child-templates/` files aren't discoverable by name with Read-only access, but the protocol fully specifies every bundle file's shape, so I'll author from that spec.)\n\nLet me first record my observation work (E-A). Solving the graph:\n\n- **Graph**: 7 vertices, 9 edges. Degree-3 vertices are {v2,v3,v4,v5}; the rest are degree 2.\n- **Lower bound k ≥ 4**: a size-3 cover would have to cover 9 edges with 3 vertices of max degree 3, forcing all three to be degree-3 and pairwise non-adjacent (zero internal edges). Among {v2,v3,v4,v5} the only non-adjacent pairs are {v2,v5} and {v3,v4}; no triple is pairwise non-adjacent. So no size-3 cover exists.\n- **k = 4**, and the minimum covers are exactly the complements of the size-3 independent sets. The size-3 independent sets are {v1,v4,v7}, {v1,v5,v6}, {v2,v5,v6}, {v3,v4,v7}, giving **4 minimum covers**.\n\nThis is E-A. Now I'll author the child bundle (E-B) and all deliverables."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1805,"cache_read_input_tokens":39901,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1805},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8843aec-ea9b-4e6a-b241-21caf2273747","uuid":"5c04bafa-a39c-48c3-9a38-903c6375c6a5","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:13:27.836Z","request_id":"req_011CdsYWbceA9rUGFh5W6mZv"}
